{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9a05caa70ddee519", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# AudioMosaic: Contrastive Masked Audio Representation Learning\narXiv: 2605.14231\nAuthors: Hanxun Huang, Qizhou Wang, Xingjun Ma, Cihang Xie, Christopher Leckie, Sarah Erfani\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. AudioMosaic introduces a contrastive audio pre-training framework that uses structured time-frequency masking to construct complementary positive pairs for effective and efficient spectrogram-based learning.\n  2. A representation-level analysis using effective rank demonstrates that structured time-frequency masking prevents dimension collapse by reducing shared local redundancy between positive pairs.\n  3. AudioMosaic achieves state-of-the-art performance on multiple audio benchmarks, supports memory-efficient large-batch pre-training, and improves audio-language models when integrated as an audio encoder.\n\nTags: SSL, SSL/对比式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ef98fad1-77b7-4ffa-931d-599a6a8e0455", "uuid": "8ec08ac0-4212-4e9a-a051-2367b9731c9f", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T07:18:09.657Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# AudioMosaic: Contrastive Masked Audio Representation Learning\narXiv: 2605.14231\nAuthors: Hanxun Huang, Qizhou Wang, Xingjun Ma, Cihang Xie, Christopher Leckie, Sarah Erfani\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. AudioMosaic introduces a contrastive audio pre-training framework that uses structured time-frequency masking to construct complementary positive pairs for effective and efficient spectrogram-based learning.\n  2. A representation-level analysis using effective rank demonstrates that structured time-frequency masking prevents dimension collapse by reducing shared local redundancy between positive pairs.\n  3. AudioMosaic achieves state-of-the-art performance on multiple audio benchmarks, supports memory-efficient large-batch pre-training, and improves audio-language models when integrated as an audio encoder.\n\nTags: SSL, SSL/对比式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b0721f86e617430f", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Rethinking Masking Strategies for Masked Prediction-based Audio Self-supervised Learning\narXiv: 2603.23810\nAuthors: Daisuke Niizumi, Daiki Takeuchi, Masahiro Yasuda, Binh Thien Nguyen, Noboru Harada, Nobutaka Ono\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_representation\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We clarify the impact of masking strategies on audio spectrogram-based representation learning, highlighting their effects across different downstream tasks.\n  2. We propose DWM, a lightweight masking strategy tailored to audio spectrograms, which leverages dispersion patterns with minimal additional computational cost.\n\nTags: SSL, SSL/预测式-离散", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "ef98fad1-77b7-4ffa-931d-599a6a8e0455", "uuid": "33611263-a0b7-4da8-864d-b03baaa35f23", "timestamp": "2026-08-12T07:18:09.935Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Rethinking Masking Strategies for Masked Prediction-based Audio Self-supervised Learning\narXiv: 2603.23810\nAuthors: Daisuke Niizumi, Daiki Takeuchi, Masahiro Yasuda, Binh Thien Nguyen, Noboru Harada, Nobutaka Ono\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_representation\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We clarify the impact of masking strategies on audio spectrogram-based representation learning, highlighting their effects across different downstream tasks.\n  2. We propose DWM, a lightweight masking strategy tailored to audio spectrograms, which leverages dispersion patterns with minimal additional computational cost.\n\nTags: SSL, SSL/预测式-离散", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
